  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/luciocephalus-aura-2/",
      "html": "<p>The pikeheads (Luciocephalus) are highly specialized labyrinth fish. Only two species are known. The Peppermint Pikehead becomes about 10-12 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/luciocephalus-aura-2/",
      "html": "<p>Due to their feeding habits and the high demands regarding water quality, pikeheads should be kept by experienced keepers only.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/luciocephalus-aura-2/",
      "html": "<p>Only two species are known: the \"common\" pikehead, which occurs on the Malay Peninsula and in Indonesia, and the Peppermint Pikehead, which is known so far only from the Province Jambi on Sumatra.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/luciocephalus-aura-2/",
      "html": "<p>Pikeheads live as predators in blackwaters of Southeast Asia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/luciocephalus-aura-2/",
      "html": "<p>Pikeheads feed exclusively on live food, preferably shrimps, for feeder fish often transmit dangerous diseases.</p>"
    }
  ],
